      "contentType": "text",
      "media": [],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "⚡️🇺🇸 Valve has suffered a massive 12TB data leak, potentially exposing a decade of Steam game files and data from more than 2,000 games.\n\nThe leaked archive reportedly comes from Valve’s old Steam2 content server, covering data from 2003 to 2013. Reports suggest the data was not obtained through a conventional hack, but was allegedly exposed through an unprotected public endpoint.\n\nAmong the discoveries are beta versions of Left 4 Dead 2, unreleased Portal 2 content, files linked to the cancelled Half-Life 2: Episode Three and Portal prequel F-Stop, as well as cut Counter-Strike content.\n\nThe leak could be one of the largest video games data leaks ever, with developers and publishers potentially affected beyond Valve itself.\n\n@medmannews",
